CraveCache 🍔🚀 — Comprehensive Functional Documentation & Verification Guide
This document provides a complete breakdown of all architectural components, portals, features, and step-by-step verification procedures for CraveCache, an AI-powered food ordering and delivery platform.
1. Architecture & Tech Stack
Frontend: React 18, TypeScript, Redux Toolkit (state management), Tailwind CSS (styling), Lucide React (icons), Motion (animations), React Toastify (notifications).
Backend: Node.js, Express, TypeScript / ES Modules, MongoDB Atlas (Mongoose ORM), Stripe Payment Gateway, Cloudinary (media management), Socket.IO (real-time order tracking & updates).
AI Integration: Google GenAI SDK (@google/genai) for intelligent meal recommendations, smart search, and dietary preference matching.
2. Core Portals & User Roles
CraveCache supports three distinct user roles with dedicated workflows and dashboards:
Customer Portal: Browse restaurants, explore AI recommendations, filter cuisines, customize dishes, manage cart, checkout with Stripe, track live orders, and review past orders.
Restaurant Owner Portal: Manage menus, toggle dish availability, accept/reject incoming orders, update kitchen preparation stages (Pending → Preparing → Out for Delivery → Delivered), and view restaurant analytics.
Super Admin Dashboard: Oversee platform-wide analytics, manage user accounts (customer/owner/admin roles), approve restaurants, and monitor platform health.
3. Detailed Features & Functionalities
🍕 A. Customer Experience & Discovery
Landing & Home Page (LandingPage.tsx, HomePage.tsx):
Hero banner with quick search by dish or restaurant name.
Cuisine category filters (Fast Food, Italian, Asian, Desserts, Healthy, etc.).
Featured restaurants with ratings, delivery time estimates, and tags.
AI Food Assistant & Recommendation Engine (AIFoodAssistant.tsx, AIRecommendationEngine.tsx):
AI-powered chat/prompt interface where users can ask for personalized meal suggestions based on mood, dietary restrictions (vegan, keto, gluten-free), or budget.
Smart recommendations card displaying curated dishes with instant "Add to Cart" actions.
Food Customization (FoodCustomizerModal.tsx):
Options to choose portion size (Regular, Large), add extra toppings/cheese, remove ingredients, and add special cooking instructions.
🛒 B. Cart, Checkout & Payments (CartDrawer.tsx, CheckoutPage.tsx)
Slide-over cart drawer displaying itemized bills, delivery instructions, tip selector, and promo code application.
Secure Checkout page with delivery address form and Stripe payment integration.
Automatic inventory validation and order placement triggering real-time Socket.IO notifications to restaurant owners.
🚴 C. Live Order Tracking (OrderTrackerModal.tsx, OrdersPage.tsx)
Interactive step-by-step progress tracker for active orders:
Order Placed
Kitchen Preparing
Out for Delivery
Delivered
Order history with status badges, item details, reorder capability, and rating/feedback submission.
🧑‍🍳 D. Restaurant Owner Portal (OwnerPortalPage.tsx)
Live Order Queue: Accept or reject incoming customer orders instantly with audio/visual alerts.
Menu Management: Add new food items, update prices, upload images, and toggle item availability (In Stock / Sold Out).
Kitchen Status Updates: Advance order status from Preparing to Out for Delivery with a single click.
🛡️ E. Super Admin Dashboard (AdminDashboardPage.tsx)
Platform-wide statistics (Total Orders, Revenue, Active Restaurants, Registered Users).
User Management table with role assignment (customer, owner, admin) and account controls.
Restaurant approval workflow and platform analytics charts.
4. Step-by-Step Verification & Testing Checklist
Use this checklist to verify that every part of CraveCache is working correctly:
Feature / Module	Verification Steps	Expected Result
1. User Authentication	Click "Sign In / Register", select role (Customer / Owner / Admin), and submit mock/real credentials.	Modal closes, user state updates in Redux, and correct navbar/portal options appear.
2. Restaurant Discovery	Browse the Home page, click on a restaurant card to view menu items.	Navigates to RestaurantDetailsPage showing restaurant header, ratings, and categorized food items.
3. AI Recommendations	Open the AI Assistant widget, type a preference (e.g., "Suggest spicy dinner under $15").	AI returns personalized recommendations with instant add-to-cart buttons.
4. Food Customization	Click on any food item card to open the customizer modal. Select size, add toppings, and add to cart.	Item with custom options is successfully added to the slide-over cart drawer.
5. Checkout & Payment	Open Cart, proceed to Checkout, enter delivery address, and complete payment.	Order is placed successfully, redirected to Orders page with active tracking status.
6. Live Order Tracking	Open OrdersPage or click on the active order tracker.	Live progress bar updates in real time as order states change.
7. Owner Portal	Log in as a Restaurant Owner. Go to Owner Portal.	View incoming orders in the queue, click "Accept" and advance order status to "Preparing".
8. Admin Dashboard	Log in as Super Admin. Navigate to Admin Dashboard.	View platform metrics, review revenue graphs, and manage user roles/restaurants.
5. API & Backend Health Check
Health Endpoint: GET /api/health returns { status: "ok" }.
WebSocket Connection: Socket.IO connects automatically on app load for instant order updates between customers, kitchens, and delivery riders.
